00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:13.970
Virginia, a rooster's call brings the farm to life.

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:18.660
On this sleepy day, the farm's newest inhabitants are slow to greet the morning.

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:41.510
But every new day promises a series of fresh adventures full of endless possibilities.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:52.910
Just days old, a newborn calf seizes the opportunity to reaffirm its bond with its mother.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:08.160
Tucked away in the safety of a barn, a litter of kittens hone their predatory skills.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:28.200
In the corner of her pen, a mother hog sings a lullaby to her nursing young.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:49.920
Nine little piglets, four weeks old, are raised on the sounds of their mother's voice.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:55.920
Nursing is an energetic event, with each piglet usually laying claim to a single nipple.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:04.500
In the safety of their pen, these piglets will be sheltered and protected.

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:08.790
But life is a lot more tenuous for those babies born in the wild.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:19.150
Many ways of coming into the world.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:24.190
And each baby's entrance is both unique and extraordinary.

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:40.210
Some babies start life without the help of a parent.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:42.680
Tiny and independent.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:48.260
They arrive with the instinct they need to survive on their own.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:51.590
A hatchling turtle will never know its mother.

00:05:51.590 --> 00:06:00.000
And within minutes of birth, it is prepared to embark on a lifetime journey.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.540
Brooding out as an egg doesn't always mean going it alone.

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:10.640
For up to 40 days, this penguin father shares brooding duties with mom.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:20.140
He'll sit for weeks at a time, enduring hunger and cold for his chick's survival.

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:26.310
But no animal invests as much in the care of its young as the mammal.

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:30.000
This giant panda will hold her newborn for 25 years.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:37.810
days, going without food or water. Her cub will rely on its mother through the third year of its

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:49.080
life. Other mammals are born larger and more developed. And in the case of this buffalo calf,

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:55.280
it's a good thing. He'll have to keep up with the herd within hours of birth.

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:10.170
For mammals, the process of birth is notoriously difficult, but nature takes no chances.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:16.330
The act of delivery triggers a boost of hormones that puts her in the mood for motherhood.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:28.320
A visual bond, too. A pattern found in youngsters of many species that evokes a nurturing response.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:33.730
Big head, big eyes, little noses.

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:38.990
The visual stamp we call cute is etched in our genes.

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:49.910
Chemistry at work as well.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:55.120
A youngster's unique scent will make a powerful imprint on mother's memory.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:00.000
And nursing cements this all-important bond.

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:20.370
- On a crowded beach, an instant bond

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:22.870
between mother and child can mean the difference

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:27.650
between life and death.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:30.000
At the height of the birthing season,

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.980
Thousands of Cape Fur seals are born here.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:03.820
Here, danger often arrives on the heels of birth.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:12.340
Nearly one-third of each new generation will die in the first months of life.

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:25.960
Thanks to a zealously protective mother, this one looks like it just might make it.

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:36.210
easily be lost in such a large crowd. So its mother wastes no time in getting to know her

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:46.290
newborn. She memorizes his unique smell and distinct bark. The pup soon gets to work at

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:53.300
what he knows best, making the most of their short time together. Every moment this mother

00:09:53.300 --> 00:10:00.000
spends on land, she will go without food, making sure that her pup has a steady supply of her

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:07.900
milk. Youngster's gain

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:09.480
has been his mom's loss.

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:11.850
When she can bear her hunger

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:14.120
no longer, she will leave for the

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:15.460
open seas to feed.

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:19.850
If she stays, both she

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:21.930
and her little one will die of

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:30.000
hunger. So though she has spent

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:35.910
less than a week with her newborn she heads into the surf her pup tries to

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:53.190
follow but a fur seal pup this young cannot swim crowded beach is not a safe

00:10:53.190 --> 00:11:00.000
haven for a lonesome pup instinctively he seeks out the company of others his

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:06.260
own size, where there is safety in numbers, and companionship to help pass the time till

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:07.260
mom returns.

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:24.530
There are places in the world where a mother needs to stick by her young for years.

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:30.000
In the freezing temperature of the northern latitudes, a female polar bear emerges from

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:37.200
She has spent five months buried beneath the snowy slopes without eating.

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:41.280
By now, she has lost nearly half of her body weight.

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:54.630
From her long fast, she hesitates, testing the air for trouble, and soon reveals the reason for her caution.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:11.140
three months ago a tiny polar bear cub takes his first peek at the world around

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:26.160
him his twin not far behind in spite of her hunger the family will remain at the

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:30.000
den for several days her cubs are still too young to

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:40.300
venture car. Curious about everything. Even a snowball offers up a unique first experience.

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:49.310
The more precocious brother knows exactly what to do with this frozen delicacy.

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:06.560
In one fell swoop, mother pulls them back into the safety of the den.

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:10.120
Their world is a dangerous place.

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:46.180
kill cubs. And mother polar bears have died, defending their young. The cubs born here die

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:51.690
in their first year. But these little ones don't yet know the perils beyond their den.

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:59.920
For the first few days, the cubs will explore their immediate surroundings.

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:07.570
Mom grows impatient to hunt, but her cubs are still too weak to keep up.

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:17.060
First, they must develop their snow legs, a daunting task on the tricky ice.

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:30.000
Their mother can no longer ignore her hunger, and soon the

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:40.380
family heads out in search of food. They will seek out their fate on the open ice. Their story

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:55.130
has just begun. The babies also begin their lives as buried treasures, but they will have to do

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:58.010
without a fierce half-ton of a mother guardian.

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:06.560
Far to the south lie the warmer shores of a Florida beach.

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:17.450
Here two months ago, a mother ended a 10-year pilgrimage to the beach of her own birth.

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:19.900
She left something precious behind.

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:26.480
A clutch of tiny loggerhead turtles buried two feet deep.

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:30.000
The whole group has scrabbled madly for three days to

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:39.890
their way out. They are greeted with a blinding layer of sand, but this is no deterrent. Once

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:47.850
above ground, their instinct tells them to head for the water. Like tiny bumper cars in

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:55.210
a race, over 100 brothers and sisters prod and bump each other onward. Each turtle swept

00:15:55.210 --> 00:16:00.000
up in the surging rush towards the sea.

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:08.120
They will eventually take their place among the ocean's great giants, weighing nearly 400 pounds.

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:15.210
Though for now, their two-inch-long bodies make the distance to the water a marathon.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:43.030
to be left behind, the last loggerhead races to meet the surf. She and her siblings have

00:16:43.030 --> 00:16:48.480
already parted ways, for it is the fate of the sea turtle to travel alone.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:17:00.000
At sea, her voyage has only just begun.

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:05.730
she points towards the safety of the deep and will not rest until she reaches the distant

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:19.360
if lonely haven of the gulf stream infants journeys could be less lonely than that of

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:28.640
the african elephant on this day a long-awaited occasion is celebrated on the savannah

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:41.460
After 22 months in her mother's womb, a calf is born into the herd.

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:50.890
She will spend the first two years of life close to her mother's side.

00:17:50.890 --> 00:17:56.760
Yet this baby will also be raised by an extended family of aunts, cousins, and sisters.

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:11.500
Her first shaky steps are quickly reassured by the entire herd.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:20.910
She is touched by every member of her new family.

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:39.700
As a female, this calf can look forward to a lifetime of protection amongst these gentle giants.

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:09.900
Like humans, elephant calves spend their long childhood learning the ways of their kind.

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:30.000
Young males playfully test their skills.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:36.180
strength with each other in preparation for the day they become adults and leave the herd

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:54.040
to make it on their own.

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:59.760
In the midst of such a caring and vigilant herd, there is plenty of room for play.

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:18.960
Reptiles are not known for their nurturing ways, of course.

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:23.080
But sometimes the most cold-blooded of mothers can surprise us.

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:29.490
In the murky bank of a Florida swamp, another newcomer is about to enter the world.

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:41.890
Having spent sixty days in the safety of an eggshell, the alligator hatchling digs its

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:53.240
way out, and takes a first look at its new surroundings.

00:20:53.240 --> 00:20:57.240
It appears she is about to receive a not so warm welcome.

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:30.000
the jaws of life not death it seems even the

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:38.470
most feared of predators can have a soft spot for her young. Between her razor-sharp

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:46.540
teeth, she gently ferries her babies to the shore, one by one, depositing them in their

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:56.210
new home. Life in the gator hole is risky for all young gators, but mom will keep a

00:21:56.210 --> 00:22:00.000
watchful eye over them for a whole year, never strained.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:13.440
too far. Infancy, after all, is a perilous time. Yet, oddly enough, a baby's helplessness

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:22.290
might be its most valuable asset. Some creatures are born into the world clinging on for dear

00:22:22.290 --> 00:22:27.400
life. They will eventually learn to let go of their parents.

00:22:30.670 --> 00:22:35.730
But for now, their tight grasp has an overpowering influence over their mothers.

00:22:35.730 --> 00:22:45.180
Their total dependency and vulnerability work to evoke the most basic nurturing instinct.

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:04.900
But it's not just their mothers who are charmed.

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:11.550
The set of physical proportions and facial features we call cute

00:23:11.550 --> 00:23:16.990
cuts across the species barrier to tug at human hearts.

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:25.760
Creatures quite unlike us have that unmistakable appeal.

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:38.420
But for all the oohing and eyeing, cuteness is actually a deadly serious business.

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:45.560
It's no coincidence that the cutest young are often the ones most dependent on parental care.

00:23:54.060 --> 00:23:59.980
Evolution has been perfecting infants for millions of years for the sole purpose of making mom...

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:07.760
go that extra mile to keep baby alive a mother might find her infant

00:24:07.760 --> 00:24:16.120
irresistible now but looks alone won't get you through life survival means

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:28.100
mastering the ways of the world and the rules of your kind mother will not

00:24:28.100 --> 00:24:29.540
always be around

00:24:33.360 --> 00:24:39.430
But following in her steps, a youngster will begin to learn the most amazing things.

00:24:45.110 --> 00:24:50.350
Whether in the wild, in a barn, or in a house, being a mother means being a role model.

00:24:53.690 --> 00:24:59.090
The nine little piglets born far from the wild have much to learn from their mother hog.

00:25:03.390 --> 00:25:07.800
Here in the shelter of their pens, they are safe from predators.

00:25:07.800 --> 00:25:12.460
Humans take care of all their needs.

00:25:12.460 --> 00:25:30.000
Nevertheless, a piglet is just as curious as its wild cousins are.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:35.760
babies seem to think their moms are impressive everything she does is worthy

00:25:35.760 --> 00:25:42.980
of imitating following her lead they soon discover their snouts have a

00:25:42.980 --> 00:25:51.190
purpose an exceptional sense of smell helps a piglet uncover buried delicacies

00:25:51.190 --> 00:25:56.860
but this little one is too young to actually eat what she might find for now

00:25:56.860 --> 00:26:00.000
chewing is just a game and a fun way of discussing

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:08.600
discovering what pigs are supposed to eat. But life on a farm is a far cry from growing

00:26:08.600 --> 00:26:18.760
up in the wild, where there is more at stake.

00:26:18.760 --> 00:26:30.000
The polar bear twins are now a year older, each weighing 200 pounds. Still nursing,

00:26:30.250 --> 00:26:33.650
Their mother must kill every few days to keep them fed.

00:26:33.650 --> 00:26:41.120
But soon they will have to feed themselves and she must show them how.

00:26:41.120 --> 00:26:50.480
Her keen sense of smell has picked up a bearded seal pup under the ice.

00:26:50.480 --> 00:26:57.290
With the highly evolved stealth and cunning of a great hunter,

00:26:57.290 --> 00:26:59.960
she silently closes in on her victim.

00:27:24.570 --> 00:27:27.910
are a little too eager and are not as light on their feet.

00:27:38.440 --> 00:27:42.760
Habitaging a mother bear's hunt is not the best way to make it through adolescence,

00:27:43.370 --> 00:27:46.570
but imitating her hunting technique may be.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:42.530
appears to be sheer frolic is a serious lesson in ice hunting.

00:28:42.530 --> 00:28:47.250
The young cubs might think it's just a game, but they are actually practicing what every

00:28:47.250 --> 00:28:55.030
polar bear adult knows: there are good things to eat under the ice.

00:29:16.800 --> 00:29:25.630
From the Arctic to the African tropics, mother's dietary lessons are the key to survival.

00:29:25.630 --> 00:29:30.000
Here the chimpanzee has perfected the art of tool use using hammers.

00:29:30.030 --> 00:29:34.910
to crack hard-shelled nuts.

00:29:34.910 --> 00:29:38.370
Nutcracking is the job of grown-ups,

00:29:38.370 --> 00:29:52.750
a skill that can take 10 years to perfect.

00:29:52.750 --> 00:30:00.000
Babies might be great at imitating,

00:30:00.440 --> 00:30:03.300
But this one is a little too young to handle the job.

00:30:06.600 --> 00:30:14.380
With her infant by her side,

00:30:14.770 --> 00:30:19.370
a mother just might succeed in encouraging her youngster to pay close attention.

00:30:24.600 --> 00:30:29.000
One determined young chimp has taken up the challenge with great enthusiasm.

00:30:30.510 --> 00:30:33.370
But tool use is a tough nut to crack.

00:30:39.470 --> 00:30:47.540
Her whimpers of frustration alert mom who steps in to demonstrate how it works.

00:31:04.510 --> 00:31:16.670
She succeeds at last, her efforts richly rewarded.

00:31:16.670 --> 00:31:21.230
Our closest relatives in the animal kingdom might remind us of ourselves.

00:31:21.230 --> 00:31:23.240
Tool use is just the beginning.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:35.920
In humans, a chimpanzee mother's ties to her young are unusually strong and long-lasting.

00:31:35.920 --> 00:31:49.960
In chimp society, each mother practices her own unique style of parenting.

00:31:49.960 --> 00:31:53.970
This first-time mom keeps her newborn pressed close to her side.

00:32:01.080 --> 00:32:03.980
she will gently cuddle and comfort her little one,

00:32:03.980 --> 00:32:13.980
instantly responding to even the tiniest whimper.

00:32:13.980 --> 00:32:15.520
Extremely protective,

00:32:15.520 --> 00:32:22.060
she is cautious about allowing others near her baby.

00:32:22.060 --> 00:32:23.960
But the new addition to the family

00:32:23.960 --> 00:32:29.160
quickly becomes the center of attention,

00:32:29.160 --> 00:32:30.000
especially for

00:32:30.090 --> 00:32:40.310
siblings that can't keep their hands off the little one. A more experienced mom is

00:32:40.310 --> 00:32:46.310
a little more comfortable with the responsibilities of motherhood. Left to

00:32:46.310 --> 00:32:53.390
his own devices, her baby is free to explore the world around him. Here, amongst

00:32:53.390 --> 00:32:58.260
such mothers, infancy is a relatively carefree time for chimps.

00:33:01.760 --> 00:33:08.290
And yet, with so much care invested in their children, creatures like chimps risk devastating loss.

00:33:15.880 --> 00:33:19.960
On this day, a young chimpanzee is dying in the forest.

00:33:26.440 --> 00:33:29.300
Its mother seeks refuge for the two of them in a tree.

00:33:30.090 --> 00:33:34.970
Her baby is too weak to cling on to her, and she must carry it the only way she can.

00:33:45.160 --> 00:33:53.040
With her infant is deep, and she refuses to let it go.

00:34:05.920 --> 00:34:12.760
Finally, with a gesture so like that of our own species, she gently bids her baby a last

00:34:12.760 --> 00:34:25.360
farewell.

00:34:25.360 --> 00:34:28.450
We cannot know how animals feel about one another.

00:34:30.120 --> 00:34:34.580
or what might be going through the mind of a chimpanzee.

00:34:34.580 --> 00:34:36.360
And yet, at times,

00:34:36.360 --> 00:34:43.470
their behavior invites us to draw our own conclusions.

00:34:43.470 --> 00:34:45.280
Such dedicated mothers

00:34:45.280 --> 00:34:49.690
may not guarantee a long life for all youngsters,

00:34:49.690 --> 00:34:51.270
but they do make childhood

00:34:51.270 --> 00:34:54.580
a relatively carefree time for most.

00:35:13.310 --> 00:35:18.500
Baby chimps are fortunate to have intelligent, powerful, devoted mothers.

00:35:18.500 --> 00:35:28.480
But in the wild, devotion comes in all shapes and sizes.

00:35:36.040 --> 00:35:42.040
Some mothers are called upon to stand up to the most terrifying of predators, to defend their young.

00:35:42.040 --> 00:35:59.210
A newly hatched brood of eider ducklings is closely guarded by their mom, cleverly concealed in a warm nest of her down.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:08.910
These youngsters are too young to fly and are at their most vulnerable, for this starving

00:36:08.910 --> 00:36:17.040
polar bear, even the tiniest morsel, is worth the effort of catching it.

00:36:17.040 --> 00:36:23.850
She stands by her brood, her duckling's feathers are barely dry, and if they take to the sea,

00:36:23.850 --> 00:36:28.740
they could drown, but she knows she is no match for a polar bear.

00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:35.800
Sometimes discretion is the better part of valor.

00:36:35.800 --> 00:36:42.770
An arctic tern sits tight on her nest.

00:36:42.770 --> 00:36:50.100
Her chicks are still not airworthy,

00:36:50.100 --> 00:36:53.300
but their tiny mother is not too comfortable on the ground.

00:36:53.300 --> 00:37:00.000
In the face of the enemy, she takes flight.

00:37:00.730 --> 00:37:05.150
becoming part of a graceful and intimidating force.

00:37:05.150 --> 00:37:10.200
Once airborne, they mount a vigorous assault,

00:37:10.200 --> 00:37:18.260
striking the bear where it is most vulnerable.

00:37:18.260 --> 00:37:26.200
This time, the bear will have to stay hungry.

00:37:26.200 --> 00:37:30.000
Today, the young hatchlings have been spared a grim

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:35.260
fate but soon the day will come when their mother will no longer need to

00:37:35.260 --> 00:37:40.860
protect them the young terns will rise on their wings and follow their family

00:37:40.860 --> 00:37:49.610
to see the age-old instinct to protect their genes will make moms do almost

00:37:49.610 --> 00:38:00.000
anything here on a California rookery another pup awaits his mother's return

00:38:00.700 --> 00:38:08.820
A sea lion pup must fend for himself on land while its mother feeds offshore.

00:38:08.820 --> 00:38:16.520
For a helpless youngster, trouble always seems to linger close by.

00:38:16.520 --> 00:38:21.510
Fortunately, this one has attracted some unwanted attention.

00:38:32.680 --> 00:38:54.520
speedy return can save the day his only weapon is his cry for help fishing trip

00:38:54.520 --> 00:38:59.730
mother calls out for her baby but instead of hearing his reply

00:39:00.280 --> 00:39:12.790
She is greeted by the loud din on the noisy rookery, trains to hear his distinct bark, a sound imprinted on her at the moment of birth.

00:39:12.790 --> 00:39:30.000
Not a moment too soon, she hears his call. The gull is foiled, and her youngster is rescued.

00:39:37.550 --> 00:39:42.540
It will be nearly a year before this pup can survive on its own.

00:39:42.540 --> 00:39:48.600
In the meantime, the little family wastes no time in reaffirming its ties to one another.

00:40:04.000 --> 00:40:09.450
as babies grow more independent of their mothers they must rely on their own instinct to get by

00:40:11.090 --> 00:40:18.730
in a forest of central china a young panda is beginning to explore the world around her

00:40:18.730 --> 00:40:30.000
pandas are by nature solitary creatures although this toddler still relies on its mother mom doesn't stray far she keeps

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:39.190
keeps busy feeding around the clock, and will consume 80 pounds of bamboo today.

00:40:39.190 --> 00:40:45.400
Like any toddler, the cub is curious about everything, and left to her own devices, she

00:40:45.400 --> 00:40:53.280
is all too eager to sample the world through her mouth.

00:40:53.280 --> 00:40:58.230
With mother so distracted by her hunger, the cub slips away to play by herself.

00:41:02.170 --> 00:41:05.270
Trees quickly become a great source of entertainment.

00:41:06.810 --> 00:41:10.740
Stink tells her they are also important for safety.

00:41:12.420 --> 00:41:16.700
But in order to hide in a tree, she must first learn to climb it.

00:41:22.790 --> 00:41:30.000
Mother seems unconcerned about her adventurous but well-padded yarn.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:41.430
youngster. She will eventually master daring feats of acrobatics, although for now, her

00:41:41.430 --> 00:42:00.000
performance seems a little unsteady. In another part of the world, other rambunctious youngsters are

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:11.680
also fine-tuning their tree climbing skills. Black bear cubs face a tenuous survival in

00:42:11.680 --> 00:42:18.840
the wild, especially vulnerable to adult male bears. Their best chance of escaping is the

00:42:18.840 --> 00:42:24.830
safe haven of a tree, and a crash course in climbing just might be the answer.

00:42:45.230 --> 00:42:50.840
soon takes over when one youngster thinks she's found a perfect spot for a winter's den.

00:43:01.500 --> 00:43:03.970
A nosy sister soon follows her act.

00:43:03.970 --> 00:43:08.520
Sibling rivalry is by no means confined to human children.

00:43:08.520 --> 00:43:26.760
Investigating every nook and cranny, no hollow must be left unexplored.

00:43:32.940 --> 00:43:37.640
Some youngsters, the most valuable lesson is learning to get along with one another.

00:43:39.220 --> 00:43:42.080
Baboons spend their entire lives in troops.

00:43:44.000 --> 00:43:48.120
Out of necessity, they learn the rules of their society pretty quickly.

00:43:54.580 --> 00:43:56.960
Very young enjoy a privileged position.

00:43:58.220 --> 00:44:00.000
As babies, they are exempt.

00:44:00.030 --> 00:44:06.190
from the rules, at least for the time being.

00:44:06.190 --> 00:44:10.010
Their older siblings, however, have no excuses.

00:44:10.010 --> 00:44:13.160
When growing up in a hierarchy, social graces

00:44:13.160 --> 00:44:17.380
are quickly learned and practiced.

00:44:17.380 --> 00:44:21.020
Young ones navigate through the strict rules of society

00:44:21.020 --> 00:44:26.770
by communicating a sign of respect to adults.

00:44:26.770 --> 00:44:30.000
They present themselves in a show of submission.

00:44:30.380 --> 00:44:38.090
even when just passing through.

00:44:38.090 --> 00:45:00.000
Applying baboon etiquette to other species can sometimes be a little confusing.

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:10.280
social status of a turtle, this young baboon is not taking any chances. Apparently, some species

00:45:10.280 --> 00:45:20.800
are born with absolutely no social graces. A baby's curiosity about foreign species is bound

00:45:20.800 --> 00:45:30.000
to make life a little more interesting. A busy intersection of an African waterhole provides an endless source

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:43.330
of entertainment for all, wide open to new experiences, a youngster's journey

00:45:43.330 --> 00:45:51.640
through life is full of strange encounters and untold possibilities.

00:46:07.640 --> 00:46:15.560
When novelty fails to present itself, the young create it for themselves by getting into all sorts of mischief.

00:46:15.560 --> 00:46:27.590
These pups may think they are on to something, though what they do not know is that coyotes generally don't hunt badgers.

00:46:30.030 --> 00:46:54.610
An extraordinary fighting machine, a badger is clever and crafty, undaunted, the pups make a comeback, practicing the oldest coyote trick in the book, teamwork.

00:47:00.380 --> 00:47:16.380
the lucky badger gets away, leaving the pups howling. Some youngsters are born ruffians,

00:47:16.700 --> 00:47:30.000
ready to mug another species at the drop of a hat. With a nose for trouble and an

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:37.230
empty stomach. A black bear yearling and her sister investigate a hornet's nest with predictable

00:47:37.230 --> 00:47:47.650
results. Nosiness can sometimes land one in trouble, as these unfortunate cubs have just

00:47:47.650 --> 00:47:56.320
learned the hard way. But her nagging hunger won't let her give up. A fearless attack,

00:47:56.660 --> 00:48:00.000
Though somewhat shaky technique, seems to do the trick.

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:06.750
trick. Another skill has been mastered, and the sisters are soon rewarded with a tasty

00:48:06.750 --> 00:48:16.560
pile of hornet's grubs. Whether you're a cub or a calf, the impulse to play comes naturally.

00:48:18.310 --> 00:48:30.000
Play seems to be an end unto itself.

00:48:30.410 --> 00:48:36.310
with no apparent purpose, but to keep oneself entertained.

00:48:36.310 --> 00:48:44.970
Other times, play looks like a simple celebration,

00:48:44.970 --> 00:48:48.340
to be shared with others your own size.

00:48:48.340 --> 00:48:52.420
And yet, these random acts of silliness

00:48:52.420 --> 00:48:55.270
are not without their purpose.

00:48:55.270 --> 00:48:58.660
These juvenile males are just play fighting.

00:48:58.660 --> 00:49:00.000
But today's play may

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:07.890
be the basis for tomorrow's new world order play is also a way of developing

00:49:07.890 --> 00:49:17.100
motor skills building endurance and learning to flee from danger here on the

00:49:17.100 --> 00:49:22.940
farm a game of king of the mountain is all good fun but in the play of these

00:49:22.940 --> 00:49:28.180
rambunctious little goats lies their ancestors nimble ways of escaping

00:49:28.180 --> 00:49:30.000
predators

00:49:51.820 --> 00:49:57.060
While the young prey sharpen their escape skills, the terrifying predators of the barn

00:49:57.060 --> 00:50:00.000
are honing the art of the stalk and the attack.

00:50:16.350 --> 00:50:17.730
Locked in a deadly duel,

00:50:18.300 --> 00:50:22.000
kitties soon discover the art of finding the perfect vantage point.

00:50:25.910 --> 00:50:26.670
It's a surprise.

00:50:40.520 --> 00:50:47.970
belong to that very special place in life. A place full of strange and wonderful experiences.

00:50:51.350 --> 00:50:57.730
A place called childhood, where every twist and turn in the road will shape a young creature's life.

00:51:27.160 --> 00:51:30.000
It is the world warmed by the nurturing attentions

00:51:30.030 --> 00:51:48.010
a parent where life is greeted with the most reassuring of gestures it is full

00:51:48.010 --> 00:51:52.340
of scary encounters and unexpected tenderness

00:52:09.280 --> 00:52:20.130
It is a solo voyage piloted by instinct and patterned by circumstance.

00:52:20.130 --> 00:52:25.380
For all, it is a feast of first encounters and new discoveries.

00:52:33.450 --> 00:52:37.650
where ordinary events are experienced through fresh young eyes.

00:52:37.650 --> 00:52:54.550
It is a time when lessons are mastered and learning is rewarded.

00:53:03.390 --> 00:53:07.950
A place where the joy of youth is shared with creatures of your own kind.

00:53:07.950 --> 00:53:19.490
Sometimes, in the company of an entire family.

00:53:30.250 --> 00:54:00.000
"And whether growing up takes a period of days or years, eventually a youngster will have the urge to leave the protection of its nest, den or herd, to start life on its own. They, too, will have their own young."

